{"abstract":"Tomitigate security risks of Internet voting, techniques for verifiability have been developed, allowing the voters to verify that their cast vote has not been manipulated. One such technique is the use of tracking codes, which does not rely on complex cryptographic mechanisms, and therefore is often assumed to be more intuitive for the voters. However, no systematic evaluation of the usability, verification efficacy, and perceived trustworthiness of these systems has yet been conducted. Our contribution evaluates two variants of a tracking code-based system in a user study (N = 306), testing both of the variants in the absence of vote manipulations as well as using different simulated tactics of vote manipulation. We conclude that both of our proposed variants are perceived as easy to use, transparent, and trustworthy in the absence of vote manipulation. However, we found varying rates of verification efficacy based on the vote manipulation tactic, manipulation with detection rates ranging from 0% to 76%. We conclude that using tracking codes can be a viable approach. At the same time, more awareness of potential manipulations needs to be raised to achieve the required security level, irrespective of the verification technique in place.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nissen, Christina Frederikke","Kulyk, Oksana","Volkamer, Melanie","Fredrich, Lara Elisabeth","Hermansen, Helena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798530"],"event":{"acronym":"E-VOTE-ID","title":"International Joint Conference on Electronic Voting"},"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karlsruher Institut für Technologie"],"keyword":["Manipulation detection","Usability","User study","end to end verifiability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tracking code based verification design and evaluation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108830857/B1-6.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798530","ids":["itu-5679a1f5-9128-4dc4-9ca5-447247d47922"],"keyword":["end-to-end verifiability","manipulation detection","tracking code-based verification","usability","user study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-645DCCE4BCE31EEA1F730AABD0A6B407"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108830857/B1-6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"karlsruher institut für technologie","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Karlsruher Institut für Technologie","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Frederikke","key":"nissenpau","last":"Nissen","locid":"a4d5d125-061e-4594-b4e4-1389a19ff99f","name":"Nissen, Christina Frederikke","orcid":"0009-0005-7912-9249","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oksana","key":"kulykpau","last":"Kulyk","locid":"1dbd1112-eb47-4406-936c-6807e8845610","name":"Kulyk, Oksana","orcid":"0000-0003-4218-1658","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Melanie","key":"volkamerpau","last":"Volkamer","name":"Volkamer, Melanie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lara Elisabeth","key":"fredrichpau","last":"Fredrich","name":"Fredrich, Lara Elisabeth","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Helena","key":"hermansenpau","last":"Hermansen","name":"Hermansen, Helena","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Gesellschaft für Informatik","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Ninth International Joint Conference on Electronic Voting (E-Vote-ID 2024)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5679a1f5-9128-4dc4-9ca5-447247d47922"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tracking Code-based Verification-Design and Evaluation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798530","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This study investigates remote voting preferences, the trade-off between vote secrecy and integrity, and vote verification among the Albanian electorate using an online survey. The results show that remote voting through an internet voting system is the preferred option. The findings also reveal the importance of ensuring vote secrecy while prioritizing vote integrity, supported by participants’ preferences for vote verification. This study contributes with insights for the future design of a remote voting system that could foster public trust among the Albanian electorate.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Budurushi, Jurlind","Faraon, Montathar","Agbesi, Samuel","Kulyk, Oksana","Dalela, Asmita"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798566"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duale Hochschule Baden-Württemberg","Kristianstad University"],"keyword":["Integrity","Preferences","Secrecy","Verification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"voting beyond borders a pilot study investigating preferences and trade offs in remote voting among the albanian electorate","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108830650/paper16.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798566","ids":["itu-e8f9b13f-9379-4ed3-9caf-36effa1a489a"],"keyword":["Integrity","Preferences","Remote voting","Secrecy","Verification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-79F0628A9B0C38E16BD9E80FE13A02D0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108830650/paper16.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"duale hochschule baden württemberg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Duale Hochschule Baden-Württemberg","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kristianstad university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Kristianstad University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jurlind","key":"budurushipau","last":"Budurushi","name":"Budurushi, Jurlind","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Montathar","key":"faraonpau","last":"Faraon","name":"Faraon, Montathar","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Samuel","key":"agbesipau","last":"Agbesi","name":"Agbesi, Samuel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Oksana","key":"kulykpau","last":"Kulyk","locid":"1dbd1112-eb47-4406-936c-6807e8845610","name":"Kulyk, Oksana","orcid":"0000-0003-4218-1658","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Asmita","key":"dalelapau","last":"Dalela","name":"Dalela, Asmita","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of Ongoing Research, Practitioners, Posters, Workshops, and Projects of the International Conference EGOV-CeDEM-ePart 2024. CEUR Workshop Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e8f9b13f-9379-4ed3-9caf-36effa1a489a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Voting beyond borders: A pilot study investigating preferences and trade-offs in remote voting among the Albanian electorate","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798566","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"A lack of transparency in internet voting systems – in particular, how the integrity of the election result is ensured – has been commonly mentioned as one of the main barriers to its adoption. We conduct an empirical study ( = 940) evaluating the factors affecting the voters’ perception of transparency and trust in an internet voting system. Thereby, we adopt a proposal from prior research that conceptualizes transparency as consisting of several individual dimensions. Our study shows that the transparency dimensions of information availability, understandability, and verifiability have a significant positive effect on voters’ perception towards the general transparency of the voting system, and also that transparency has a positive effect on trust in the system. In addition, we investigate how the information presented about the system and the procedures available to voters for verifying the integrity of their cast vote affects voters’ perception of transparency and trust in the system. We find that providing technical documentation about the system significantly increases perceived transparency and trust. We conclude that while such information is unlikely to be understood by most voters, it effectively signals the possibility of expert audits of the system.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Agbesi, Samuel","Budurushi, Jurlind","Dalela, Asmita","Nissen, Christina Frederikke","Kulyk, Oksana"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798571"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duale Hochschule Baden-Württemberg"],"keyword":["Internet voting","Transparency","Trust","Verifiability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to increase transparency and trust in internet voting systems an experimental study","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108831077/The_Impact_of_Transparency_Dimension_in_Internet_Voting_System_NordiCHI.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798571","ids":["itu-fb79e060-db20-4b42-a8ea-74b8c3b2d025"],"keyword":["Internet Voting","Transparency","Trust","Verifiability","Vote Integrity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B8D178624D752BDCCF4864F33B2674A7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108831077/The_Impact_of_Transparency_Dimension_in_Internet_Voting_System_NordiCHI.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"duale hochschule baden württemberg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Duale Hochschule Baden-Württemberg","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Samuel","key":"agbesipau","last":"Agbesi","name":"Agbesi, Samuel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jurlind","key":"budurushipau","last":"Budurushi","name":"Budurushi, Jurlind","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Asmita","key":"dalelapau","last":"Dalela","name":"Dalela, Asmita","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Frederikke","key":"nissenpau","last":"Nissen","locid":"a4d5d125-061e-4594-b4e4-1389a19ff99f","name":"Nissen, Christina Frederikke","orcid":"0009-0005-7912-9249","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oksana","key":"kulykpau","last":"Kulyk","locid":"1dbd1112-eb47-4406-936c-6807e8845610","name":"Kulyk, Oksana","orcid":"0000-0003-4218-1658","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 13th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fb79e060-db20-4b42-a8ea-74b8c3b2d025"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How to increase transparency and trust in internet voting systems: An experimental study","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798571","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"While cookie disclaimers on websites have been proposed to ensure that users make informed decisions regarding consenting to data collection via cookies, such informed consent is hindered by several factors. One of them is the presence of so-called dark patterns, that is, design elements that are used to lead users to accept more cookies than needed and more than they are aware of. The second factor is lack of transparency on behalf of the service providers with regards to what happens if the user does not consent to cookie usage even despite dark patterns nudging them to do so. The contributions of this paper are (1) evaluating the efficacy of several of these factors while measuring actual behaviour; (2) identifying users' attitude towards cookie disclaimers including how they decide which cookies to accept or reject; (3) assessing the behaviour of websites regarding storing non-necessary cookies despite user's consent. We show that different visual representation of the reject/accept option have a significant impact on users' decision. We also found that the labelling of the reject option has a significant impact. In addition, we confirm previous research regarding biasing text (which has no significant impact on users' decision). Our results on users' attitude towards cookie disclaimers indicate that for several user groups the design of the disclaimer only plays a secondary role when it comes to decision making. We furthermore show that even without user's explicit consent, the majority of websites we investigated still uses non-necessary cookies. We provide recommendations on how to improve the situation for different stakeholders, namely, for developers and policy makers.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Berens, Benjamin","Bohlender, Mark","Dietmann, Heike","Krisam, Chiara","Kulyk, Oksana","Volkamer, Melanie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798557"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karlsruhe Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Cookies","Dark patterns","Privacy","User study","Web tracking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cookie disclaimers dark patterns and lack of transparency","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cose.2023.103507","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798557","identifier":[{"id":"85174302261","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ca8baf1a-f99e-4739-aad8-90951cd043f7"],"keyword":["Cookies","Dark patterns","Privacy","User study","Web tracking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-55E147AD1E3F3711942334C59BEB1E1B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cose.2023.103507","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108830401/ARES_2022_Cookies_Extended.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"karlsruhe institute of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Benjamin","key":"berenspau","last":"Berens","name":"Berens, Benjamin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"bohlenderpau","last":"Bohlender","name":"Bohlender, Mark","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Heike","key":"dietmannpau","last":"Dietmann","name":"Dietmann, Heike","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chiara","key":"krisampau","last":"Krisam","name":"Krisam, Chiara","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Oksana","key":"kulykpau","last":"Kulyk","locid":"1dbd1112-eb47-4406-936c-6807e8845610","name":"Kulyk, Oksana","orcid":"0000-0003-4218-1658","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Melanie","key":"volkamerpau","last":"Volkamer","name":"Volkamer, Melanie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cose.2023.103507","issn":["01674048","18726208"],"issn_org":["01674048"],"journal":"Computers & Security","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Computers & Security","volume":"136"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85174302261"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ca8baf1a-f99e-4739-aad8-90951cd043f7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cookie disclaimers: Dark patterns and lack of transparency","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798557","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Online service users sometimes need support when making privacy-related decisions. Humans make decisions either slowly, by painstakingly consulting all possible information, or quickly, by relying on cues to trigger heuristics. Human emotions elicited by the decision context affects decisions, often without the decision maker being aware of it. We wanted to determine how an information-based decision can be supported, and also to understand which cues are used by a heuristics-based approach. Our first study enhanced understanding of underlying encryption mechanisms using metaphors. Our participants objected to efforts to make them ‘technical experts’, expressing a need for reassurance instead. We fed their free-text responses into a Q-sort, to determine which cues they rely on to make heuristic-based decisions. We confirmed the desire for reassurance. Our third study elicited ‘cyber stories’: Unprompted narratives about cyber-related experiences to detect emotional undertones in this domain. Responses revealed a general negativity, which is bound to influence cybersecurity-related decisions.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kulyk, Oksana","Renaud, Karen","Costica, Stephan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718848"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["South Africa","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Abertay University","All Global Affiliations","Rhodes University","University of South Africa","University of Strathclyde"],"keyword":["Cyber","Decision making","Privacy","Reassurance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"people want reassurance when making privacy related decisions not technicalities","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jss.2023.111620","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718848","identifier":[{"id":"85148538445","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-456894ee-16ea-4e1b-800a-d0930e44dee4"],"keyword":["Cyber","Decision-making","Privacy","Reassurance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-11BBC28986B67D516E5F8067C2089F62"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jss.2023.111620","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102802987/main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0164121223000158","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of strathclyde","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Strathclyde","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"za","key":"rhodes university","loc":["South Africa","Africa"],"name":"Rhodes University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"za","key":"university of south africa","loc":["South Africa","Africa"],"name":"University of South Africa","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"abertay university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Abertay University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oksana","key":"kulykpau","last":"Kulyk","locid":"1dbd1112-eb47-4406-936c-6807e8845610","name":"Kulyk, Oksana","orcid":"0000-0003-4218-1658","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"renaudpau","last":"Renaud","name":"Renaud, Karen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stephan","key":"costicapau","last":"Costica","name":"Costica, Stephan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jss.2023.111620","issn":["01641212","18731228"],"issn_org":["01641212"],"issue":"111620","journal":"Journal of Systems and Software","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Systems and Software","volume":"200"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148538445"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-456894ee-16ea-4e1b-800a-d0930e44dee4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"People want reassurance when making privacy-related decisions—Not technicalities","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718848","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Context: Data protection regulations such as the GDPR and the CCPA affect how software may handle the personal data of its users and how consent for handling of such data may be given. Prior literature focused on how this works in operation, but lacks a perspective of the impact on the software development process. Objective: Within our work, we will address this gap and explore how software development itself is impacted. We want to understand which data protection-related issues are reported, who reports them, and how developers react to such issues. Method: We will conduct an exploratory study based on issues that are reported with respect to data protection in open source software on GitHub. We will determine the roles of the actors involved, the status of such issues, and we use inductive coding to understand the data protection issues. We qualitatively analyze the issues as part of the inductive coding and further explore the reasoning for resolutions. We quantitatively analyze the relation between the roles, resolutions, and data protection issues to understand correlations.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Henning, Anne","Schulte, Lukas","Herbold, Steffen","Kulyk, Oksana","Mayer, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718895"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karlsruher Institut für Technologie","University of Passau"],"keyword":["CCPA","Data protection","GDPR","Open source software","Software development"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"understanding issues related to personal data and data protection in open source projects on github","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2304.06367","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718895","ids":["itu-93c8a24a-e3bf-4041-b91b-a667daf2be25"],"keyword":["CCPA","Data Protection","GDPR","Open Source Software","Software Development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-0DFFB932110972E9B2AAD654BBA86256"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2304.06367","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2304.06367.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.06367","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"karlsruher institut für technologie","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Karlsruher Institut für Technologie","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of passau","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Passau","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"henningpau","last":"Henning","name":"Henning, Anne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lukas","key":"schultepau","last":"Schulte","name":"Schulte, Lukas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"herboldpau","last":"Herbold","name":"Herbold, Steffen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Oksana","key":"kulykpau","last":"Kulyk","locid":"1dbd1112-eb47-4406-936c-6807e8845610","name":"Kulyk, Oksana","orcid":"0000-0003-4218-1658","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"mayerpau","last":"Mayer","name":"Mayer, Peter","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2304.06367","status":"p","title":"Registered Report with Continuity Acceptance (CA) for submission to Empirical Software Engineering granted by RR-Committee of the MSR'23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-93c8a24a-e3bf-4041-b91b-a667daf2be25"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Understanding issues related to personal data and data protection in open source projects on GitHub","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718895","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"While Internet voting is argued to have the potential to improve election processes, concerns about security risks remain one of its main adoption barriers. These concerns are furthermore aggravated by the lack of transparency of Internet voting systems that are often perceived as a “black box”. Moreover, there is a research gap in conceptualizing the idea of transparency and in studying voters’ attitudes towards transparency in Internet voting. In this work, we aim to address this gap by (1) Conducting a systematic literature review, from which we identified five dimensions of transparency; (2) Developing a questionnaire (Transparency Dimensions of Internet Voting, TDIV) to assess voters’ attitudes regarding the correlation of these dimensions with transparency; and (3) Conducting an online study (N = 500) to investigate voters’ attitudes towards transparency in Internet voting. We conclude that providing information about the security of the Internet voting system; testing it by independent experts for security vulnerabilities prior to the election; monitoring the election process and verifying its integrity; and providing a remedy for security breaches while holding the responsible parties accountable, are perceived by voters as important, and enhance transparency in Internet voting systems.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Agbesi, Samuel","Dalela, Asmita","Budurushi, Jurlind","Kulyk, Oksana"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718844"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Internet voting","Security risks","Systematic literature review","Transparency","Voter attitudes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigating transparency dimensions for internet voting","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102788628/Investigating_Transparency_Dimensions_for_Internet_Voting.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718844","identifier":[{"id":"85174542017","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-42787808-611d-48a6-bdde-468d13957ff6"],"keyword":["Internet voting","Security risks","Systematic literature review","Transparency","Voter attitudes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-81740A59DFC3C6DFAC19A429DB574C22"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-43756-4_1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102788628/Investigating_Transparency_Dimensions_for_Internet_Voting.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Samuel","key":"agbesipau","last":"Agbesi","name":"Agbesi, Samuel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Asmita","key":"dalelapau","last":"Dalela","name":"Dalela, Asmita","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jurlind","key":"budurushipau","last":"Budurushi","name":"Budurushi, Jurlind","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oksana","key":"kulykpau","last":"Kulyk","locid":"1dbd1112-eb47-4406-936c-6807e8845610","name":"Kulyk, Oksana","orcid":"0000-0003-4218-1658","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9783031437564"],"isbn":["9783031437557"],"pages":"1-17","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"International Joint Conference on Electronic Voting","volume":"14230"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85174542017"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-42787808-611d-48a6-bdde-468d13957ff6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Investigating Transparency Dimensions for Internet Voting","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718844","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Denmark is one of the most digitised countries in Europe. However, according to recent reports, IT security in Danish companies has not followed along. To shed light into the challenges that companies experience with implementing IT security, we conducted interviews with four employees from four different companies, asking about their IT security and their needs to become better protected. Our results show that the companies are lacking fundamental security protection and are in need of basic security help and raising awareness of cyber threats in the organisations. Based on our findings, we discuss directions for future steps in terms of addressing these issues.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fleron, Camilla Nadja","Jørgensen, Jonas Kofod","Kulyk, Oksana","Paja, Elda"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712517"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cyber Threat Awareness","Digitalisation","Fundamental Security Protection","IT Security","Security Implementation Challenges"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-AAF","DI-PR-ALL"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-AAF","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards a basic security framework for smes results from an investigation of cybersecurity challenges in denmark","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85174678778","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712517","identifier":[{"id":"85174678778","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-48cc02f5-690d-4dc6-9ff1-c18d6a740d72"],"keyword":["Cyber Threat Awareness","Digitalisation","Fundamental Security Protection","IT Security","Security Implementation Challenges"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Techno